Berry-FCM-OS7 includes or references the following third-party components:

- libadb-android (https://github.com/MuntashirAkon/libadb-android), used by the Android APK as a Maven/JitPack dependency. Upstream is dual-licensed GPL-3.0-or-later OR Apache-2.0. This project uses the Apache-2.0 option where applicable. See the upstream repository for the full license texts and dependency notices.
- Conscrypt Android (https://github.com/google/conscrypt), Apache-2.0.
- FCM Socket 443 matching design was informed by the public FCMFix ColorOS project (https://github.com/ByteJuno/fcmfix-coloros, MIT); no LSPosed hook source is copied into this project.

The original Berry-FCM KernelSU module LICENSE is retained in the module package.

- Google Material Icons (https://github.com/google/material-design-icons), Apache-2.0. Selected SVG paths are converted to Android VectorDrawable resources for in-app module/navigation icons. The BerryFCM adaptive launcher icon is original to this repository.

- Priv Kit 0.20.0 (https://github.com/priv-kit/priv-kit/tree/v0.20.0), distributed as io.github.priv-kit:priv-core. Its upstream Maven publication declares Apache License 2.0. License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt. Used for an independent authorized Binder command service; the app's existing ADB key is used only for startup.
- Shizuku API / provider (https://github.com/RikkaApps/Shizuku-API), MIT, optional external authorization mode.
